  "prompt": "OK from the top! Sasha's ass ain't the only thing shaking, but the damn whole room with her off-key caterwauling.\n\"BABY, DON'T GO,\" she belts out, not even pretending to follow the melody you've painstakingly laid down in your home studio. Tasha's supposed to be on backup vocals, but she's too busy trying to twerk against the speaker, her thick thighs smacking together with each off-beat thrust. Keisha's supposed to be on the hook, but she's scrolling through her phone, occasionally mumbling something that might be a lyric if you squint your ears hard enough. And Mia... well, Mia is at least trying, but her eyes keep darting to the door like she's expecting the cops to raid the studio instead of just their impromptu recording session.\nYou lean back in your chair, the worn leather groaning under your weight. You've been at this for three hours, and the only thing you've recorded is a masterclass in how not to make a hit track. Your patience is wearing thinner than the last dollar in your pocket, and that's saying something. The beat thumps through the floorboards, a solid, steady rhythm that's the only thing holding this mess together. You grab the mixing board's fader, sliding it down until Sasha's screeching fades to a tolerable hum.\n\"Aight, that's enough,\" you say, your voice cutting through the noise. All four of them freeze, Sasha's mouth hanging open mid-note. Tasha stops her gyrations, nearly toppling over. Keisha looks up from her phone, and Mia blinks like she's just woken up. The silence that falls is heavier than any of their asses combined. You fix each of them with a stare, letting the disappointment settle in the room. \"You call yourselves performers? My grandma's got more rhythm than all of you put together, and she's been dead ten years.\" You gesture towards the door. \"Get the hell out. All of you. Come back when you remember how to follow a damn beat.\"\nThe silence in the studio stretches, thick and uncomfortable. Sasha's the first to break it, her braids swinging as she plants her hands on her ridiculous hips. \"Hell no, Kato. You ain't kicking us out. Your wack-ass beat got us all messed up anyway.\" She juts her chin out, defiant. \"Maybe if you made something worth listening to, we could actually get into it.\"\nBefore you can even form a response to that, Keisha pipes up from her corner, not even bothering to look up from her phone. \"He right though, Sasha. That shit do sound weak. Like some nursery rhyme bullshit.\" She finally glances at you, a smirk playing on her lips. \"What happened? Did you lose your touch, old man?\"\nTasha, who's been uncharacteristically quiet, sashays over to you. The scent of her cheap perfume and something warmer, uniquely her, fills the space between you. She stops just a little too close, her caramel-tinted thigh brushing against your jeans. \"Don't be like that, Daddy Kato,\" she purrs, her voice a low, teasing rumble. \"We're just... not feeling the vibe right now.\" She reaches out, her fingers trailing over the mixing board, dangerously close to your own. \"Maybe you need to relax a little. Help us find the right... inspiration.\" Only Mia seems to have taken your words to heart, standing off to the side with her arms wrapped around herself, looking genuinely contrite. Her big brown eyes dart from her bickering sisters back to you, her plush bottom lip caught between her teeth. The tension in the room has shifted from frustration to something else entirely, a volatile mix of challenge and flirtation, all pointed directly at you. The beat you made, the one you were so proud of, now seems like a distant memory.\n{ She brought her friends }\nJust as you're about to lay down the law, the studio door creaks open, interrupting the standoff. In struts Francesca, followed by two other girls you recognize from the club, all of them carrying that unmistakable energy of women who've just come from a long night of attention and cash. Francesca takes in the scene with a quick, knowing sweep of her eyes—your tense posture, Sasha's defiant stance, Tasha pressed against you. A small smile plays on her lips as she leans against the doorframe, crossing her arms.\n\"Well now,\" Francesca says, her voice smooth as aged whiskey. \"Sounds like y'all are having a real productive session in here.\" Her eyes land on you, and there's a challenge in them that matches her friends'. \"Don't tell me the great producer Kato is having trouble handling the Ward sisters.\"\nSasha immediately preens at the arrival of her friend, her back straightening. \"Girl, you have no idea. He's trippin' over here with this weak-ass beat, acting like we the problem.\" She gestures wildly at the mixing board. \"Then he had the nerve to try and kick us out! Him! The one with the wack production!\"\nKeisha's friend, a petite dancer named Monae with bright green hair, plops down on the worn leather sofa, kicking her feet up. \"Damn, Kato,\" she calls out, not an ounce of respect in her tone. \"Heard you was losing your touch, but I ain't know it was this bad.\" Her eyes rake over you, bold and appraising. \"Maybe you need some new talent to inspire you. These girls clearly forgot how to bring the heat.\"\nThe studio, once your domain, now feels invaded, packed with too many bodies, too many attitudes. Your space has been transformed into a clubhouse of defiant women, all looking at you with varying degrees of challenge and amusement. The beat continues to thump softly in the background, a steady reminder of the work that was supposed to get done tonight, now completely derailed. Tasha presses a little closer, her heat seeping through your clothes, while Francesca watches it all unfold from her perch by the door, her expression unreadable.\n\n",
